{"author":{"id":"b409816c5cd5ab140d1d52eb33aace35de44952bb794b19806fd57f6ecb1ace9"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1792611707,"nonce":"obSUznl1+j1mOMxohgVqa6OxESA=","title":"TypeScript: accept TSX and JavaScript checking inputs with explicit native semantics","message":"The pinned official conformance folder contains TSX and JavaScript inputs, which the current adapter explicitly inventories and skips. The native parser uses SourceType::ts() and project support focuses on executable .ts sources.\n\nSupport source-kind selection and checking of TSX/JS where requested, including file extensions, JSDoc/checkJs/allowJs and JSX factory/intrinsic typing. Native JSX execution needs a chosen callable/object model; this is not a request to transpile product code into browser JavaScript. Keep check-only support distinct from native execution coverage. Resolve shared module/project integration instead of silently dropping these files.\n\nUntil supported, these are coverage skips, not conformance passes. Driver directive support and multi-root handling remain under 63f459c5d2cf4b513599a90423637eee9adf5faa296254a5e4cb139c152eeb87.\n\nEvidence: official TypeScript conformance corpus at 3e9236361fa97a9e6c685f4833ac457ae2d8c50a, oracle 7.1.0-beta, native d978fe3fa5f8f7480d0c0d1b7dd2ca4548b490f0. This is check-only acceptance/category comparison under strict defaults, not JIT/runtime coverage. The full affected-case inventory will be attached after the complete audited run. Parent: 6875fc2949f83d682861ecab814e0ff82c824f5990620b0d64ca0340ebb026e5.","files":null}]}